The exact script `tools/interop.zig` and the files above call
`reference_params.sage` is HorizenLabs' `poseidon2_rust_params.sage`
(https://github.com/HorizenLabs/poseidon2, file last changed in commit
`bb476b9ca38198cf5092487283c8b8c5d4317c4e`; repository licensed MIT OR
Apache-2.0), SHA-256
`c301c6d074b58cc27f117f59971f405a16c57d10e6140f1025643fa25ba75223`, verified
byte-identical on 2026-09-17. It is not vendored here; fetch it from there.

`tools/subspace_trail.py` is a SECOND port of the same acceptance checks, on
sympy, written to cross-check the Zig one; it is this repository's own file
(MIT) and reproduces no sage source verbatim, but it is derived from the same
script and is named here for that reason. It is a test instrument: nothing in
the published module builds it or runs it, and `zig build test-poseidon` never
spawns it — `src/mds_replay_test.zig` replays a captured transcript instead.

Deliberate divergences from the reference are documented in `src/grain.zig`'s
module doc (rejection vs reduction in two places, and the Grain output filter's
bit consumption) and in `src/mds_security.zig`'s (the two proved rewrites, and
`check_minpoly_condition` belonging to `generate_matrix_partial` rather than to
`generate_matrix`'s acceptance loop).

## NOT reproduced here: circomlib / circomlibjs

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — circomlibjs is an ORACLE this module RUNS, not code
it ships: every number here that involves it was produced by executing it, so no
circomlib source and no circomlib data is in this repository.

`iden3/circomlibjs` (**GPL-3.0**, stated in its `package.json`) and
`iden3/circomlib` (**LGPL-3.0**, the circom circuits) are used only as
comparison targets, and only ever by being *run* or by being *digested* — never
by being copied:

* `src/vectors_test.zig`'s circomlibjs known answers are computed by
  `tools/gen_vectors.mjs`, which imports circomlibjs from a disposable clone,
  runs both its reference and its optimized implementation and requires the two
  to agree. The clone lives outside this tree (`.zig-cache/`, gitignored) and
  what the generator prints is this repository's own measurement of a black box,
  not a transcription of upstream's test file. Last regenerated 2026-09-06
  against circomlibjs 0.1.8 (`48b3ab37013c5ed21e9ff8a80a5b010795c97094`): every
  value was unchanged — Poseidon is deterministic — which is the point, since
  what the run replaced was the provenance and not the arithmetic.
* `src/constants_test.zig` pins SHA-256 digests of tables THIS module derives
  with its own Grain-LFSR port, and documents how to re-clone circomlibjs and
  recompute the comparison yourself. A digest is not the data.

Nothing at all is taken from `iden3/circomlib`; it is a design reference,
recorded as such in this module's `README.md` `Provenance:` statement and in
`SPEC.md`. No circomlib or circomlibjs source and no circomlib or circomlibjs
data is present in this repository, so their terms do not reach this module.
